# Keep secrets and cruft OUT of the build context / image.
# The Dockerfile COPYs backend/ wholesale, so a stray backend/.env would otherwise
# be baked into the image. These patterns prevent that.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.git
.gitignore
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
# Anchored patterns only match the root, and the virtualenv lives at backend/.venv, so a bare
# ".venv/" missed it entirely: every build shipped 151MB of Windows virtualenv into the context
# (115MB after compression) and the Dockerfile COPYs backend/ wholesale, so it was being baked
# into a linux/amd64 image where it cannot run anyway.
**/.venv/
**/venv/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
**/*.log
.playwright-mcp/
deploy/
docker-compose*.yml
